; SaveFOTBuilder — the recorded-call capture medium for non-principal ports
; and connections (FOTBuilder.cxx SaveFOTBuilder). The byte-level capture the
; fot backend started with is unsound for the delta-state RTF stream
; (syncCharFormat deltas, first-use font numbers), so ProcessContext captures
; CALLS: each FotSink method invoked while a connection routes elsewhere is
; recorded as a SaveCallRec (tag + deep-copied args, singly-linked with a
; tail pointer — the reference Call list) and replayed through the sink when
; the owner flushes. Replaying into a sink that is itself capturing simply
; re-records onto the outer queue (the reference's emit-into-SaveFOTBuilder
; splice, expressed as a re-record — payload copies land on the outer
; queue's host, which is what keeps them alive across brackets).
;
; RBMM: all records and payload copies live on the queue's own `host` (the
; owner's region — it outlives the deeper node brackets that connect).
; charactersFromNode keeps the RAW grove data pointer (the reference does
; not copy it — grove storage is run-lived and pointer adjacency drives the
; fot text-run regrouping); characters() copies (the reference builds a
; StringC).

use scaly.memory.Page
use scaly.containers.Array
use opensp.StringC.StringC
use dazzle.Grove.GroveNode
use dazzle.Style.InheritedC
use dazzle.Style.DisplayNIC
use dazzle.Style.RuleNICRec
use dazzle.Style.LinkNICRec
use dazzle.Style.GraphicNICRec
